<title>THAILAND: Thai sugar vessel movements on May 7.</title>
<headline>Thai sugar vessel movements on May 7.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Independent surveyors detailed Thai sugar freight movement as follows (in tonne tel quels):</p>
<p>Vessel		  Position	  Quantity    Destination</p>
<p>Bismihitala	  SLD Apr 28	  9,600	Mombasa</p>
<p>Alam Teladan	 SLD Apr 30	 16,800	Malaysia</p>
<p>Tropical Rose	SLD Apr 29	  1,500	Cambodia</p>
<p>Hanbonn Brother    SLD May 04	 13,500	Indonesia</p>
<p>Saint John	   SLD May 01	 14,000	S.Korea</p>
<p>Ban Ann		SLD Apr 30	 14,100	S.Korea</p>
<p>Topaz		  SLD May 01	 13,350	S.Korea</p>
<p>Chile		  SLD May 06	  3,350	Maputo</p>
<p>Myoh Yang 3	  SLD May 05	  2,895	N.Korea</p>
<p>Kwan Mo Bong	 SLD May 05	  8,000	China</p>
<p>Jilin		  ETD May 07	 11,000	Indonesia</p>
<p>Alam Tenaga	  N/A		  15,000	Malaysia</p>
<p>Sin Hung 2	   ETD May 03	 12,500	Bangladesh</p>
<p>Bangbunnak	   ETD May 09	  5,500	Indonesia</p>
<p>Jin Cheng Jiang    ETD May 07	 14,000	China</p>
<p>Naftolos	     N/A		  18,000	Japan</p>
<p>Tolich		 ETD May 08	 12,500	Indonesia</p>
<p>Rio Venture	  ETB May 08	 16,800	Malaysia</p>
<p>Bangramard	   ETB May 08	  5,500	Indonesia</p>
<p>Yick Zao	     ETA May 06	 29,400	S.Korea</p>
<p>Kapitan Bubliskiy  ETB May 06	  9,500	S.Korea</p>
<p>Sea Harvest	  N/A		  14,000	S.Korea</p>
<p>Pu Cheng	     ETA May 11	 14,000	China</p>
<p>Sonamai		ETA May 26-30     1,300	Cambodia</p>
<p>Galactica	    ETA May 07	 14,200	Indonesia</p>
<p>Alam Taba	    ETA May 09	 15,000	Malaysia</p>
<p>Kassos		 ETA May 10-20    16,000	S.Korea</p>
<p>NOTE: SLD indicates that the vessel has left, ETA = Estimated Time of Arrival, ETD = Estimated Time of Departure, ETR = Estimated Time of Readiness, L/CAN indicated period when vessels are expected in for loading or be cancelled.</p>
